{
	quest.02306C4616627B02.quest_desc: ["It uses &cFE&r instead of fuel like Coal to smelt items."]
	quest.03F585616CDC979A.quest_desc: ["To make &lUnstable Ingots&r, you will need a &cDivision Sigil&r. They are occasionally dropped by Withers, or can be found as loot in Strongholds, Mineshafts, Dungeons, and Temples in deserts."]
	quest.053ACC174F0D1E46.quest_desc: ["&3Ender Lilies&r are occasionally found in &3The End&r's outer islands, and may be used to grow Ender Pearls.\\n\\nThey do NOT like to be watered by Watering Cans, and will teleport away. They also dislike Bone Meal, and will regress their growth if used on them. They do not mind Reinforced Watering Cans, though.\\n\\nThey grow much faster on &3Ender Cores&r."]
	quest.0712DD2EAE8FE53C.quest_desc: ["The Wind Mill's &9GP&r generation oscillates between 0.5 and 2.5. Rain increases &9GP&r generated by 1. Thunder increases &9GP&r generated by 2."]
	quest.07609654842FA968.quest_desc: ["The &3Ender Generator&r uses Ender Pearls or Eyes of Ender to generate &cFE&r."]
	quest.07609654842FA968.quest_subtitle: "Teleporting"
	quest.08AF237C41E4AEF9.quest_desc: ["The Death Generator uses loot from Undead mobs to generate &cFE&r. It will also apply the Doom effect to nearby entities while it operates, killing them in 1 minute unless cured with Milk."]
	quest.08AF237C41E4AEF9.quest_subtitle: "13th Tarot"
	quest.08CF0F0BC5B82681.quest_desc: ["The Potions Generator uses Potions to generate &cFE&r. The more complex the Potion is, the more &cFE&r will be generated."]
	quest.08CF0F0BC5B82681.quest_subtitle: "Brew Darrymore"
	quest.0951A1A3FC49AEBC.quest_desc: ["The &cResonator&r can transform certain items, occupying a variable amount of &9GP&r in the process."]
	quest.0AAA8E411D877A63.quest_desc: ["The &bQuantum Quarry&r has three slots, which can hold the following:\\nA Biome Marker, to make the &bQuarry&r prioritize the biome set on it (only works with Overworld biomes).\\nEnchanted Books: Applies the effect of the enchantment to the &bQuarry&r (example: Efficiency makes the &bQuarry&r faster, Fortune increases ore value).\\nItem Filter: Allows you to filter what items are accepted by the &bQuarry&r. All items not on the filter are voided."]
	quest.0AAA8E411D877A63.title: "Quantum Quarry Modifiers"
	quest.0F94689A7F6709FA.quest_desc: ["&aMagical Wood&r is used as a crafting ingredient for certain things, and also counts as 5 Bookshelves in one (also grants &a10 Eterna (Max 30)&r)."]
	quest.1339E6B956AA0744.quest_desc: ["It crushes things, such as flowers into dye, carpets into string."]
	quest.1408F665D8E66289.quest_desc: [
		"&cEnergy Transfer Nodes&r move energy from the attached block to blocks adjacent to either it or connected Transfer Pipes. &cEnergy Retrieval Nodes&r move energy from blocks connected to it through Transfer Pipes or directly adjacent to it to the attached block."
		"{image:atm:textures/questpics/excessiveutilities/energy_transfer_node.png width:200 height:125 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.14D6614F0FD61549.quest_desc: ["The &lHealing Axe&r will occasionally feed you a bit while held. When you attack an entity with this Axe, they will be healed, at the cost of your own health. This interaction deals increased damage to undead mobs instead. It's also unbreakable."]
	quest.16AA1B9379753CC9.quest_desc: ["Drops of Evil sometimes drop from Wither Skeletons."]
	quest.1876ADF135DEF33B.quest_desc: ["&l&eExcessive Utilities&r adds &cForge Energy&r generators as well.\\n\\nSpeed Upgrades are compatible with Generators as well, increasing their &cFE&r output up to 64 times while consuming their respective fuel type faster, at the cost of &9Grid Power&r (don't worry the generators don't use &9GP&r without these upgrades)."]
	quest.1876ADF135DEF33B.title: "FE Generators"
	quest.18CF6BE2AB854289.quest_desc: ["Cursed Earth can be made by using a Drop of Evil on Dirt. It spawns hostile mobs rapidly. If it lights on fire, it spreads rapidly to other nearby Cursed Earth, burning them into Dirt."]
	quest.18CF6BE2AB854289.title: "Cursed Earth"
	quest.1954642BB8E8C5C8.quest_desc: ["When eaten, it resets the options offered by an &5Enchanting Table&r."]
	quest.19FEB11411AA2C66.quest_desc: ["The Ring of the Flying Squid is an upgrade to the Chicken Wing Ring, allowing you to thrust yourself upward while holding SPACE (by default). The ring occupies 16 &9GP&r during this process. Additionally, like its predecessor, it can only work while it has charge."]
	quest.19FEB11411AA2C66.quest_subtitle: "Limited Flight"
	quest.1B4027ADAFB83900.quest_desc: ["It's twice as good for enchanting as Magical Wood (counts as 10 Bookshelves in one block). Also grows &3Ender Lilies&r faster."]
	quest.1B4027ADAFB83900.quest_subtitle: "Not the coremod for EnderIO"
	quest.1C4E3C45ADB9DA6F.quest_desc: ["The &dHalitosis Generator&r uses the stinky Breath of an Ender Dragon to generate &cFE&r."]
	quest.1C4E3C45ADB9DA6F.quest_subtitle: "Just take a breath mint already"
	quest.1E387B934B7DBB8C.quest_desc: ["The &6Heated Redstone Generator&r is an upgrade to the &cMagmatic Generator&r. On top of &cLava&r, it now requires Redstone to generate &cFE&r, but produces more than its predecessor."]
	quest.1E387B934B7DBB8C.quest_subtitle: "C-c-c-chicken"
	quest.204C2EFF9A0A2360.quest_desc: ["The &cExplosive Generator&r uses &8Gunpowder&r or &cTNT&r to generate &cFE&r."]
	quest.204C2EFF9A0A2360.quest_subtitle: "Kaboom"
	quest.23C68F458B1571D9.quest_desc: [
		"&eItem Transfer Nodes&r move items from the attached block to blocks adjacent to either it or connected Transfer Pipes. &eItem Retrieval Nodes&r move items from blocks connected to it through Transfer Pipes or directly adjacent to it to the attached block."
		"{image:atm:textures/questpics/excessiveutilities/item_transfer_node.png width:200 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.272DC75EAFD7B9B0.quest_desc: ["The &cMagmatic Generator&r uses &cLava&r to produce &cFE&r."]
	quest.272DC75EAFD7B9B0.quest_subtitle: "L-l-l-lava"
	quest.29D6491A130B2657.quest_desc: ["Various machines, some &cForge Energy&r-consuming, some not, offered by &e&lExcessive Utilities&r."]
	quest.29D6491A130B2657.title: "Machines"
	quest.2AA309648AE573B6.quest_desc: ["Speed Upgrades make certain Excessive Utilities machines faster. However, they have a &9GP&r cost, based on how many upgrades are in the machine at once, based on the following function:\\nstackSize*(122+4*stackSize)/126\\n\\nSpeed Upgrades also have varying stack limits, based on their tier:\\n4 (Basic)\\n16 (Magical)\\n64 (Ultimate)\\n\\nSo, for a full stack of each tier, the &9GP&r cost would be 4.38, 23.62, 192, for each respective tier."]
	quest.2AA309648AE573B6.title: "Speed Upgrades"
	quest.2AF19F2FA48D2742.quest_desc: ["The &aQED&r (&aQuadratic Extrapolation Doohicky&r) is, despite looking like a Crafting Table, much different! \\n\\nYou will need at least 1 &aEnder Flux Crystal&r in a 9x9x9 Area with the &aQED&r (&aQubit Eating Dynamo&r) in the center. The more &aEnder Flux Crystal&r you have, the faster the &aQED&r (&aQuite Expensive Decoration&r) operates."]
	quest.2AF19F2FA48D2742.quest_subtitle: "Quasar/Electron Decoration"
	quest.2B4EE8B84907CC01.quest_desc: ["The Angel Block can be placed in midair, without the need for scaffolding. Useful for building while flying."]
	quest.2B5A210AA7C6FCC3.quest_desc: ["The Chicken Wing Ring allows you to slow down your fall by holding SPACE (by default). The ring occupies 1 &9GP&r during this process. Additionally, it can only work while it has charge, which depletes while slowing your fall, and recharges while unused."]
	quest.2B5A210AA7C6FCC3.quest_subtitle: "Barely even flight"
	quest.2BB843CB01B962A4.quest_desc: ["The &9Overclocked Generator&r is the third \"Furnace-type\" generator. It burns furnace fuel instantly, receiving all the energy at once, but is the least \"efficient\" among its piers."]
	quest.2BB843CB01B962A4.quest_subtitle: "Fast"
	quest.2EAB38B23F5171B9.quest_desc: ["The Water Mill produces 4 &9GP&r per adjacent flowing water. Does not count water source blocks, and blocks flowing on its top or bottom side."]
	quest.307F4A1E8FD8098C.quest_desc: ["&cRed Orchids&r can be planted on, and found on &cRedstone Ore&r, and, when fully grown, can be harvested to get a pile of &cRedstone Dust&r."]
	quest.348DAEB7B58443C0.quest_desc: ["By dividing an Iron Ingot with a Diamond, you will get an &lUnstable Ingot&r.\\n\\n&cDue to divisions by Diamond being equivalent to divisions by zero, the Unstable Ingot can only last for 10 seconds before exploding. Make sure to craft something with it quickly before then! Attempting to leave the crafting menu while you have this ingot will result in an early explosion, and, possibly, your demise as well.&r\\n\\n&8Unstable Ingots crafted through automation are considered \"unacceptable\", and may not be used in crafting recipes.&r\\n\\n\"Hope you are good at crafting under pressure.\" - Jonh09"]
	quest.348DAEB7B58443C0.quest_subtitle: "1337/0="
	quest.348DAEB7B58443C0.title: "Unstable Ingot"
	quest.360FFC95F4CA5338.quest_desc: ["The Culinary Generator uses food to generate &cFE&r."]
	quest.360FFC95F4CA5338.quest_subtitle: "Nom nom nom, om nom"
	quest.37B9EB97518670E6.quest_desc: ["&cRed Coal&r, when used in a furnace, will burn for 8 times as long as regular Coal, as long as 4 &9GP&r is available. Otherwise, it burns for as long as regular Coal."]
	quest.3952EA91C6467B5F.quest_desc: ["This Quest has been authored by &6AllTheMods Staff&r, or a &2Community contributor&r for use in AllTheMods Modpacks.\\n\\nAs all &6AllTheMods&r packs are licensed under &eAll Rights Reserved&r, this Quest is not allowed to be used in any public packs not released by &6AllTheMods Team&r without explicit permission.\\n\\nThis quest is intentionally hidden, if you're seeing this, you're in editing mode."]
	quest.3A51ABBA9043D617.quest_desc: ["The Lava Mill generates 2 &9GP&r if Lava is horizontally adjacent to it."]
	quest.3B7BD8408919EC8B.quest_desc: ["&eItem&r and &9Fluid&r Filters can be used to filter certain things, such as &eItem&r and &9Fluid&r Nodes. You can select up to 16 different &eItems&r/&9Fluids&r per filter. By default the filter whitelists &eItems&r/&9Fluids&r. You can even put another &eItem&r/&9Fluid&r Filter into a Filter to nest it, allowing you to filter even more stuff.\\n\\nThe following options can be applied to Filters as well:\\nInvert: Turns the filter into a blacklist.\\nUse Tags: Filters by the tags of selected &eItems&r/&9Fluids&r\\nIgnore Damage: Ignores durability damage on filtered &eItems&r. Exclusive to &eItem&r Filters.\\nIgnore All Components: Ignores all NBT/Components on &eItems&r/&9Fluids&r."]
	quest.3B7BD8408919EC8B.title: "Filters"
	quest.3FB0BE9989720FD2.quest_desc: ["The Fire Mill produces 4 &9GP&r if there is fire directly below it."]
	quest.437AA94E591D82B5.quest_desc: ["The Disenchantment Generator uses Enchanted Books to generate &cFE&r."]
	quest.437AA94E591D82B5.quest_subtitle: "This Enchantment"
	quest.447E2A8170040BFE.quest_desc: [
		"&9Fluid Transfer Nodes&r move fluids from the attached block to blocks adjacent to either it or connected Transfer Pipes. &9Fluid Retrieval Nodes&r move fluids from blocks connected to it through Transfer Pipes or directly adjacent to it to the attached block."
		"{image:atm:textures/questpics/excessiveutilities/fluid_transfer_node.png width:200 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.44B1C048770E2333.quest_desc: ["&4Demon Ingots&r can be obtained by tossing &6Gold Ingots&r into lava in &cThe Nether&r, and used to craft &4Demonically Gargantuan Drums&r."]
	quest.45E7D789F14BDCC4.quest_desc: ["The Glass Cutter allows you to break glass as though you had Silk Touch.\\n\\nThe Trowel allows blocks able to be mined faster with Shovels to be collected as though Silk Touch was used."]
	quest.45E7D789F14BDCC4.quest_subtitle: "or is it?"
	quest.45E7D789F14BDCC4.title: "Cheap Silk Touch"
	quest.464B13D89C180C88.quest_desc: ["The Dragon Egg Mill produces 500 &9GP&r if a Dragon Egg is on top of it."]
	quest.464B13D89C180C88.quest_subtitle: "The Ultimate Mill"
	quest.475C38CB8BE2DD32.quest_desc: ["&e&lExcessive Utilities&r is a continuation of &e&lExtra Utilities 1&r and &e&l2&r, offering various useful items and such. Some of you might remember the mod from older versions of modded Minecraft. Whether this is your first time seeing this mod, or your thousandth, these quests will help you get aligned with the mod."]
	quest.475C38CB8BE2DD32.title: "&l&eExcessive Utilities"
	quest.49DAA43DA7DC6F04.quest_desc: ["The &zRainbow Generator&r produces &c25 million FE/t&r &lif at least 1 of all other Generators are running simultaneously&r. You may only have 1 active &zRainbow Generator&r."]
	quest.49DAA43DA7DC6F04.quest_subtitle: "LAST JARONA!"
	quest.49DAA43DA7DC6F04.title: "&zRainbow Generator!"
	quest.4CDFDBB4A370423D.quest_desc: ["The &#FF69B4Pink Generator&r uses &#FF69B4Pink Dye&r or &#FF69B4Pink Items&r to generate &cFE&r."]
	quest.4CDFDBB4A370423D.quest_subtitle: "Protip: Make an Infinity Pink Dye Cell for this Generator"
	quest.4DD2A3F8DB678A15.quest_desc: ["Transfer Pipes are used to connect Transfer Nodes to their destinations, or Retrieval Nodes to what they pull from. This pipe can handle &eItems&r, &9Fluids&r, and &cEnergy&r at once, but does nothing without Transfer or Retrieval nodes."]
	quest.504D6F3C682E466E.quest_desc: [
		"The &c&oPseudo-Inversion Sigil&r is the unbreakable counterpart of the &cDivision Sigil&r. Acquiring it requires a particularly demanding rite.\\n\\nAt any time, you can sneak right click the Beacon with a &cDivision Sigil&r to see the next step for this rite.\\n\\n1. In &dThe End&r, provide a flat area of at least 11x11 blocks and place a Beacon in its center.\\n2. Place a chest in each of the 4 cardinal directions 5 blocks away from the Beacon.\\n3. Lay down a pattern of Redstone Dust and String in a spiral pattern, as shown in this image."
		"{image:atm:textures/questpics/excessiveutilities/pseudo_rite_example.png width:125 height:125 align:center}"
		"&cRed&r corresponds to Redstone, and &3Cyan&r corresponds to String."
		"&lNext Page ->&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"4. In each chest, insert the following contents (check the tasks of this quest to see which items are valid for each chest):\\n4.1. The Northern chest: the &o&cChildren of Fire&r, 12 unique items that are produced with a Furnace.\\n4.2. The Southern chest: the &2&oGifts of Earth&r, 12 unique items that naturally generate in the Overworld.\\n4.3. The Eastern chest: the &9&oDescendants of Water&r, 12 potions.\\n4.4. The Western chest: the &e&oSpices of Air&r, 12 unique Music Discs.\\n5. Once all the previous steps have been fulfilled, initiate the ritual through the sacrifice of an Iron Golem near the Beacon.\\n6. A wave of various hostile mobs will spawn in the area. Defeat 100 of them to invert your &cDivision Sigil&r into the &c&oPseudo-Inversion Sigil&r. The ritual will fail if you die or leave &dThe End&r while the wave is still ongoing."
	]
	quest.504D6F3C682E466E.title: "Pseudo-Inversion Sigil"
	quest.52205630EEDD8221.quest_desc: ["Flat Transfer Nodes are a variation of the Transfer Node. They can fit between blocks, and will extract from the block you placed it on, transferring items or fluids to an adjacent block. Use either another Flat Transfer Node or a Wrench to access the Flat Transfer Node. Right click to place a Filter inside, or left click to pop the Node off."]
	quest.52205630EEDD8221.quest_subtitle: "Close enough. Welcome back Transfer Labels"
	quest.585DE309D29512FA.quest_desc: ["The &dLunar Panel&r does the opposite of what the &9Solar Panel&r does. Same functionality as the Solar Panel, except it only works during nighttime instead of daytime."]
	quest.592C3B758F748C6E.quest_desc: ["Drums can hold varying amounts of fluids.\\n\\n&8Stone&r: 16 buckets (1 bucket = 1000 mB).\\n&7Iron&r: 256 buckets\\n&6Reinforced Large&r: 4 096 buckets. \\n&4Demonically Gargantuan&r: 65 536 buckets.\\n&8Bedrockium&r: 1 048 576 buckets."]
	quest.595F93FB9A7D34B5.quest_desc: ["The &bFrosty Generator&r uses &bIce&r or Snow to generate &cFE&r."]
	quest.595F93FB9A7D34B5.quest_subtitle: "Don't. Touch. THE THERMOSTAT!"
	quest.5AF1D24170DCC895.quest_desc: ["Spikes can damage mobs that come into contact with it.\\n\\nWooden: 1 damage per hit, cannot deal fatal damage, does not drop experience, does not count as player kill.\\nStone: 2 damage per hit, cannot deal fatal damage, drops experience, counts as player kill.\\nIron: 4 damage per hit, cannot deal fatal damage, drops experience, does not count as player kill\\nGolden: 2 damage per hit, can deal fatal damage, drops experience, does not count as player kill.\\nDiamond: 8 damage per hit, can deal fatal damage, drops experience, counts as player kill.\\nNetherite: 10 damage per hit, can deal fatal damage, drops experience, counts as player kill."]
	quest.5BCF082BCC4A0714.quest_desc: ["The Magnum Torch, the father of the Mega Torch from Torchmaster, prevents mob spawns in a 64 block radius around itself. Hold a Magnum Torch in your hand to see the radius of placed Magnum Torches."]
	quest.5C1D18FBB1BBF6E9.quest_desc: ["Can be used to void items, energy, and fluids, respectively."]
	quest.5C1D18FBB1BBF6E9.title: "Trash Cans"
	quest.600EC6ED1AE8AB95.quest_desc: ["These blocks and items use &9GP&r, reserving part of the available capacity while they are active. If your &9GP&r usage is higher than your &9GP&r capacity, your grid is overloaded. Overloaded &9GP&r consumers stop working until usage drops or you add more generation."]
	quest.6038714CE3699B63.quest_desc: ["The &9Magical Snow Globe&r is an entire world, contained entirely within a small glass globe.\\n\\nTo activate it, you must take it to all 3 of the following dimensions:\\n- &2Overworld&r\\n- &cNether&r\\n- &5End&r\\n\\nOnce you finish your journey, you may use the &9Snow Globe&r to craft the &bQuantum Quarry&r."]
	quest.612BCFD0BFBFC6F6.quest_desc: ["The Compound Bow is an unbreakable bow that can fire arrows without needing any in your inventory (like a Bow enchanted with Infinity). Said arrows also ignore gravity.\\n\\nThis item supports Infinite Enchantment Stacking."]
	quest.612BCFD0BFBFC6F6.quest_subtitle: "Gravity? Who gives a crap about gravity?"
	quest.623B1C7C1BE9B13B.quest_desc: ["Some things that do not fit the other categories."]
	quest.62486A3D1B896A85.quest_desc: ["The Fire Axe is an unbreakable axe that can chop down entire trees in one go.\\n\\nThis item supports Infinite Enchantment Stacking."]
	quest.62486A3D1B896A85.quest_subtitle: "Perfect for firefighters"
	quest.672F6CB4404B1A3C.quest_desc: ["The Kikoku is an unbreakable sword which can deal Soul Rending damage, reducing the Max Health of opponents struck by it.\\n\\nIt is also 10 times more likely to grant Soul Fragments when you kill a mob.\\n\\nThis item supports Infinite Enchantment Stacking."]
	quest.672F6CB4404B1A3C.quest_subtitle: "Trafalgar D. Water Law's Sword"
	quest.6A77E32457EC3140.quest_desc: ["The &lEtheric Sword&r has similar stats as the Diamond Sword, but is unbreakable. When you right click, you will gain a Soul Fragment, at the cost of your Max Health. You may use the Soul Fragment to repay your Max Health debt. Soul Fragments can also very rarely be obtained by defeating Mobs, and can even allow you to have a surplus of Max HP."]
	quest.6A77E32457EC3140.quest_subtitle: "And Soul Fragments"
	quest.6AB33864599E059A.quest_desc: [
		"Speed Upgrades: Makes the Node transfer/retrieve items faster. Check out their respective quest in the &9Grid Power&r section for more info.\\n\\nStack Upgrade: Makes &eItem&r and &9Fluid&r Nodes move an increased amount of &eItems&r/&9Fluids&r at once. 64 items/operation for &eItem&r Nodes, 1000 mB/operation for &9Fluid&r Nodes.\\n\\nWorld Interaction Upgrade: Allows for the following in-world interactions with &eItem&r and &9Fluid&r Transfer Nodes:\\nOn Cobblestone adjacent to Lava and Water sources, Cobblestone is generated.\\nOn Soul Soil adjacent to Blue Ice and Lava, Basalt is generated.\\nOn Stone adjacent to a Lava source with Water behind it, Stone is generated.\\nOn a Water source block with at least 2 other adjacent Water source blocks, Water is generated.\\n\\n&lNext Page ->&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Breadth-First Search Upgrade: Makes Nodes search Transfer Pipes from nearest to farthest. Best suited for networks with numerous short branches.\\n\\nDepth-First Search Upgrade: Makes Nodes remember the path it followed upon reaching a dead end. Useful for pipe networks with many branches. These two upgrades are mutually exclusive with each other.\\n\\nPseudo Round Robin Upgrade: Makes Nodes move on to the next destination after every succesful transfer.\\n\\n&3Ender Transmitter&r: Allows Transfer Nodes to move items, fluids, energy wirelessly, including across dimensions. Makes use of a frequency shared with an &3Ender Receiver&r.\\n\\n&3Ender Receiver&r: Allows Retrieval Nodes to receive items, fluids, and energy through the same frequency as an &3Ender Transmitter&r."
	]
	quest.6AB33864599E059A.title: "Logistics-Related Upgrades"
	quest.6CF4BCFEC9A8BACE.quest_desc: ["The &9Watering Can&r can be used to accelerate the growth of crops in an area. Right click Water to fill the &9Can&r, and hold right click to water the area. The &9Watering Can&r does not like to be used by Fake Players (Modular Routers, Clickers, etc.), and will break.\\n\\nThe &9Reinforced Watering Can&r is its upgraded form, watering in a larger area, with no water cost, and can be used by Fake Players without breaking. It comes with a certain hefty price, though."]
	quest.6CF4BCFEC9A8BACE.title: "Watering Cans"
	quest.6DA3E7DF9332B8DE.quest_desc: ["The &aSlimy Generator&r uses &aSlimeballs&r and Milk to produce &cFE&r."]
	quest.6DA3E7DF9332B8DE.quest_subtitle: "Bouncy!"
	quest.6DCDC3700202B3A5.quest_desc: ["Sickles can break certain plants in a radius, depending on their tier."]
	quest.6E3482C45E4AF3DA.quest_desc: ["Sound Mufflers mute any sound within an 8 block radius around it. This also prevents vibrations getting to Wardens and Sculk Sensors."]
	quest.6E3482C45E4AF3DA.quest_subtitle: "Just follow my moves, and sneak around"
	quest.70054D4060B8949C.quest_desc: ["The &8Survivalist Generator&r is an incredibly cheap option for producing &cFE&r. It uses the same fuel as a Furnace. It is the slowest but most \"efficient\" option among \"Furnace-Type\" generators in &eExcessive Utilities&r."]
	quest.70054D4060B8949C.quest_subtitle: "Slow"
	quest.70F9EE602AE0033C.quest_desc: ["These blocks are capable of generating &9GP&r in various ways, increasing the owner's Grid's capacity, and are owned by the player who placed them."]
	quest.71D1B0CEDA9241A3.quest_desc: ["The &lDestruction Pickaxe&r can mine stone and netherrack instantly, while also voiding it. It cannot mine anything else. It is also unbreakable."]
	quest.724006CD3818C9E5.quest_desc: ["The &5Enchanter&r requires the equivalent of 15 Bookshelves (equivalent to &a30 Eterna&r for those used to &5&lApothic Enchanting&r, shelves from that mod do not count here), as well as &cFE&r to operate. It can &5enchant&r specific items. Not gear, though."]
	quest.724401B0C60DCE7A.quest_desc: ["&e&lExcessive Utilities&r offers &f&lLogistics&r as well. Almost like &3&lIntegrated Dynamics&r' logistics, in a way.\\n\\nAttach the specific Node to where you want to take items from (or move items to if using Retrieval Nodes) and use the Pipe Wrench to configure what side doesn't connect.\\n\\nOther Wrenches do work with &e&lExcessive Utilities&r as well!"]
	quest.724401B0C60DCE7A.title: "Logistics"
	quest.73996E64F65F7C87.quest_desc: ["The &lErosion Shovel&r can be used to instantly mine dirt, sand, and gravel while also voiding it. It cannot mine anything else. It is also unbreakable."]
	quest.7635D2262741BE75.quest_desc: ["The &eAngel Ring&r grants Creative flight while worn. This requires 64 &9GP&r. Unlike its predecessors, it does not use charge, allowing you to fly freely, infinitely, so long as you are maintaining your GP."]
	quest.7635D2262741BE75.quest_subtitle: "Creative Flight"
	quest.7635D2262741BE75.title: "Angel Ring"
	quest.763BF9F230D515BF.quest_desc: ["The &lReversing Hoe&r can \"de-age\" certain blocks when used.\\n\\nExamples:\\nSand -> Gravel -> Cobblestone -> Stone\\nTerracotta -> Clay\\nMagma Block -> Lava <- Obsidian"]
	quest.7887212A36D7D1CA.quest_desc: ["&9Grid Power&r (or &9GP&r) is an alternative power type &e&lExcessive Utilities&r offers. Unlike &cForge Energy&r, &9GP&r is per player, does not move through cables, batteries, Flux Points, or any other thing normally used to transport &cFE&r."]
	quest.7887212A36D7D1CA.title: "Grid Power"
	quest.79616A764789FEDA.quest_desc: ["Opinium Cores are the embodiment of opinions.\\n\\nThey come in 9 tiers:\\n- Pathetic\\n- Mediocre\\n- Passable\\n- Decent\\n- Good\\n- Damn Good\\n- Amazing\\n- Inspiring\\n- Perfected\\n\\nA single Perfected Opinium Core requires:\\n- 1024 Red Coal\\n- 4609 Iron Ingots\\n- 2304 Gold Ingots\\n- 1152 Diamonds\\n- 576 Emeralds\\n- 32 Chorus Flowers\\n- 16 Bottles o' Enchanting\\n- 8 Elytras\\n- 4 Nether Stars"]
	quest.7A6800A767A83592.quest_desc: ["The Furnace Generator is slightly more expensive than the Survivalist counterpart. Just like Survivalist, it uses furnace fuel. It burns fuel faster, but is less \"efficient\". The middle ground of the 3 \"Furnace-type\" generators."]
	quest.7A6800A767A83592.quest_subtitle: "Middle"
	quest.7AF82ADEB07747EF.quest_desc: ["The Chandelier prevents hostile mob spawns within a 16 block radius around it. Holding one in your hand shows you the radius of placed Chandeliers."]
	quest.7B7254B1E6208F9B.quest_desc: ["The Nether Star Generator uses Nether Stars...or Firework Stars to generate &cFE&r. It will also apply the Wither effect to nearby entities in a large area while it operates."]
	quest.7B7254B1E6208F9B.quest_subtitle: "Needs Patrick and ATM Star support (not really)"
	quest.7C9F22EBA3AD673B.quest_desc: ["The Manual Mill produces 15 &9GP&r per player cranking it. Once you click it, you will automatically crank it until you look away or get too far away."]
	quest.7D0A549135F997BD.quest_desc: ["The Power Manager allows you to see where all your &9GP&r generators and consumers are."]
	quest.7D34FE128DE0A262.quest_desc: ["The &bQuantum Quarry&r is capable of mining blocks from a hypothetical dimension that may have existed (a dimension much like the Overworld).\\n\\nFor the &bQuarry&r to function, each of its sides must be surrounded by &bQuantum Quarry Actuators&r. Any of the &bActuators&r accept &cFE&r. It outputs the items it gets from the hypothetical dimension to adjacent inventories, such as Chests."]
	quest.7EE006106678065F.quest_desc: ["The &9Solar Panel&r generates 1 &9GP&r while it is daytime and has a clear line of sight to the sky. During rainy weather, output is reduced by 5%."]
	quest.7F715693079A424D.quest_desc: ["Lassos can be used to hold mobs.\\n\\n&6Golden Lasso&r can only hold passive mobs, such as livestock. &0Cursed Lasso&r can only hold hostile mobs, and only when they are at half health or less."]
	quest.7F715693079A424D.title: "Lassos"
